{"id": "EUVD-2026-76683", "enisaUuid": "4e896406-991b-3df1-a22f-1e762626ea99", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nring-buffer: Fix subbuf resize race with ring buffer readers\n\ntrace_buffer subbuf_size is read lockless in ring_buffer_read_page() and\nring_buffer_read_start(), while it can simultaneously be resized with\nring_buffer_subbuf_order_set().\n\nInstead of trace_buffer::subbuf_size, use bpage::order in\nring_buffer_read_start() and ring_buffer_read_page().\n\nIn ring_buffer_read_start(), even with resize_disabled, there is still a\npossibility of a race with a buffer modification. Hold the trace_buffer\nmutex to synchronise with any pending ring buffer order modification.\n\ntrace_buffer::subbuf_size is now actually useless, remove it. Also,\ncreate accessors rb_subbuf_capacity() and rb_page_capacity() which\nreturn the actual size available for storing events, while\nrb_subbuf_size() returns the actual subbuf page-size.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:47:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:52:24", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d666f0b8b36c0765cf19fbe6de5a7ba5a73aad9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/50f4a793c4ff24826efb0ac700989a5063cc53df", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0c7c517827a453128a8f58bfd849546a29813b27", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a5f63637890f03177146efddaba5ec7a1b4d61f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89771", "GHSA-8mw5-wv48-mphh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0249cf91-52d5-3a28-b82c-495a34397579", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "291caa46-f3c0-3dfc-96dc-15dce0a38f32", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3455504d-b128-3f53-996f-38233a99b5d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9b94daa542a8d2532f0930f01cd9aec2d19621b <8a5f63637890f03177146efddaba5ec7a1b4d61f"}, {"id": "3807fbba-060e-3a4b-b09a-4c96f803ce34", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9b94daa542a8d2532f0930f01cd9aec2d19621b <6d666f0b8b36c0765cf19fbe6de5a7ba5a73aad9"}, {"id": "46a14fe9-e0b6-3169-b9ef-48b797d0e295", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "53316a45-e6be-3125-aa69-acf483a89bb5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9b94daa542a8d2532f0930f01cd9aec2d19621b <0c7c517827a453128a8f58bfd849546a29813b27"}, {"id": "97a0e257-52d5-30c0-b631-b80770877d5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b993a4e7-d437-3725-9a25-d174348a5e8c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "c4127f79-1b13-3730-afa3-c0687b5c79a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "ce755ba4-c891-3137-b2aa-88015ab32fb6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f9b94daa542a8d2532f0930f01cd9aec2d19621b <50f4a793c4ff24826efb0ac700989a5063cc53df"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9044c0a3-9509-368c-9303-2e810bb8ffbe", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}